nford Dogs 4 (Khosla et al., 2011),Oxford flower 5","level":1,"path_id":"1~49","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":51,"section_id":"sec-1~49"},{"title":"Table 6 :","text":"6Evaluation task statistics on the QA number and average clues in each category. * The AR task is designed to evaluate refusal capability. The information in the question does not exist in the dialogue, and therefore clues are unsupported.Evaluation TasksNumber of QAs Avg. CluesFR2192.90Extract. &amp; Adapt.VS3061.91TTL3374.09TR1231.74ReasoningVR1743.05MR2062.17KR812.21Knowledge ManagementCD811.70AR*184-Overall1,7112.69","level":1,"path_id":"1~50","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":52,"section_id":"sec-1~50"},{"title":"Table 7 :","text":"7The detailed resource list of models implemented in our benchmark.For open-sourced MLLM models, we obtain the official models from their corresponding Hugging Face repositories 8 . Then, we deploy them on A100 GPUs under the Linux system with the vLLM engine 9 . For closed-sourced MLLM models, we access them via official APIs. The memory model implementation and reproduction are built based on the open-sourced memory framework MemEngine 10 (ModelVenuePaper Implement. SourceFull Memory-TextN/AN/ALinkFIFON/AN/ALinkNaiveRAGN/AN/ALinkGen. AgentUIST 2023LinkLinkReflexionNeurIPS 2023 LinkLinkMemGPTArxiv 2023LinkLinkA-MemNeurIPS 2025 LinkLinkMemoryOSEMNLP 2025 LinkLinkFull Memory-MultimodalN/AN/AN/AMuRAGEMNLP 2022 LinkN/AUniversalRAGArxiv 2025LinkLinkNGMArxiv 2025LinkLinkAUGUSTUSArxiv 2025LinkN/AA.5 Benchmark Evaluation DetailsA.5.1 Experimental Environments\n\t\t\thttps://huggingface.co\n\t\t\thttps://github.com/vllm-project/vllm\n\t\t\thttps://github.com/nuster1128/MemEngine","level":1,"path_id":"1~51","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":53,"section_id":"sec-1~51"}],"citations":[{"raw_text":"JoshAchiam\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tStevenAdler\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSandhiniAgarwal\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tLamaAhmad\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tIlgeAkkaya\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFl