mographic attributes of real individuals are repre-</cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">annotator performance, or modeling human judg-</cell><cell cols=\"8\">sented or analyzed. The benchmark and dataset</cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">ment patterns. All annotation results were used</cell><cell cols=\"8\">will be released publicly with clear documentation,</cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">only to improve data quality and benchmark reli-</cell><cell cols=\"6\">permitting use for research purposes.</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">ability, with the research focus remaining only on</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">the properties of the data, models, and evaluation</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">framework rather than on any human behavior. All</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">annotators were fully informed that the annotated</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">data would be released publicly for research pur-</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">poses. Since all annotation and verification work</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">was conducted by the author team as part of the re-</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">search process, no external recruitment or monetary</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">compensation was involved. The benchmark study</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"8\">does not involve any privacy data of real users or</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell cols=\"5\">human-subject research.</cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell></cell></row></table><note><p>Qwen-2.5-VL-7B (K=15) Full (Text) FIFO NaiveRAG Gen. Agent Reflexion MemGPT A-Mem MemoryOS Full (MM) MuRAG UniversalRAG NGM AUGUSTUS Extract. &amp; Adapt.</p><p>A.8.3 Scientific Artifacts</p><p>All data sources and models underlying the benchmark are used with explicit references and official links. Detailed information can be found in Appendix A.2.2, A.4, and A.5. The benchmark primar-</p></note></figure>\n<figure xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" type=\"table\" xml:id=\"tab_11\"><head>Table 13 :</head><label>13</label><figDesc>Benchmark performance results on Qwen-2.5-VL-7B with the retrieval number K=20. The best and second-performed memory model(s) are highlighted with orange and blue backgrounds.</figDesc><table><row><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell>F1</cell><cell>0.2376</cell><cell>0.1743</cell><cell>0.6303</cell><cell>0.3020</cell><cell>0.2391</cell><cell>0.5928</cell><cell>0.6145</cell><cell>0.6265</cell><cell>0.2150</cell><cell>0.6596</cell><cell>0.6609</cell><cell>0.6589</cell><cell>0.6216</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell></cell><cell>BLEU-1</cell><cell>0.1865</cell><cell>0.1295</cell><cell>0.5438</cell><cell>0.2366</cell><cell>0.1903</cell><cell>0.5098</cell><cell>0.5210</cell><cell>0.5396</cell><cell>0.1626</cell><cell>0.5656</cell><cell>0.5639</cell><cell>0.5813</cell><cell>0.5335</cell></row><row><cell></cell><cell>F